    "description": "A set of nested, three-dimensional circulation model output of the coastal Gulf of Alaska at 3 km resolution. ROMS was implemented tracking the FATE mooring. Dataset variables include dissolved iron, nitrate, phytoplankton, salinity, temperature, vector velocity, velocity-east, and velocity-north, velocity-up. Model output can be viewed via the PMEL Ferret FOCI LAS at http://ferret.pmel.noaa.gov/FOCI/servlets/dataset. FOCI - Fisheries-Oceanography Coordinated Investigations LAS - Liver Access Server PMEL - Pacific Marine Environmental Laboratory ROM - Regional Ocean Modeling System\n\n<p>Deposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.</p>",
    "additional_descriptions": [
      {
        "description": "<p>Purpose: To investigate residence time over Portlock Bank near Kodiak, Alaska.</p>",
        "type": {
          "id": "notes",
